      \field{abstract}{The surface reconstructions of InxGa1-xAs alloys grown by molecular beam epitaxy on the (001) surfaces of GaAs and InAs have been studied by reflection high-energy electron diffraction and scanning tunnelling microscopy. A surface phase diagram is presented for the nominally strain-free alloy as a function of substrate temperature and alloy composition, and structural models for the commonly observed 3{\texttimes} reconstructions are discussed. Two new, electronically stable structural models are described that account for the transition of the InxGa1-xAs surface alloy from a c(4{\texttimes}4) to an asymmetric 3{\texttimes} reconstruction and that are fully consistent with all current experimental evidence.}
